## Current State

Last updated: 2026-07-19 | by: Claude Code | repo @ 99426f0

### What Draftly is

A **lawyer-in-the-loop legal workflow platform for Sri Lankan legal practice**.
It has two main workflow tracks: **conveyancing** and **litigation**.
Conveyancing is the first prototype workflow because it is document-heavy,
rule-driven, and easier to evaluate; litigation is the second workflow track,
using an IRAC-style structure for later drafting and review. It is a DSE (ML +
Software Engineering) product, not a
research-only project â€” full software lifecycle, demoable at a symposium.

The core framing to preserve: **Draftly is not a form-filling PDF generator and
not a legal search engine.** It turns an unstructured legal/property document
bundle into a _verified, structured title record_, checks that record, and
generates multiple lawyer-reviewable drafts from it.

Core pipeline:

```text
Documents â†’ Extraction â†’ Linking â†’ Title graph â†’ Checks â†’ Lawyer verification â†’ Drafts
```

The differentiator vs "template filling": the template is only the final output
layer. The real work is before generation â€” reading prior deeds, extracting
facts, linking them across documents, reconstructing the chain of title,
resolving name variants, and flagging missing/inconsistent information. This is
also what makes it measurable with ML metrics.

